For a fighter class, the best way to increase damage (that I know) is
to polymorph into a monster with two weapon attacks (e.g. an Elvenking
or an Aleax). As such, you will hit twice with your weapon, without the
malus for two-weaponing.

But this is _cumulative_ with two-weaponing, so that a two-weaponing
Aleax will land four blows per turn (plus an extra kick attack). The
best combination (at least against demons) would be a Kinght (who can be
skilled in saber and skilled in two-weaponing), polymorphed into an
Aleax, and wielding a blessed +7 Grayswandir and a blessed +7 silver
saber. With the x2 bonus of Grayswandir, this means 6d8 damage for the
sabers, plus 6*7 = 42 damage for enchantment. Add to that the various
strength-based damage bonus. Against a demon, add an additional 4*4 = 16
damage for using blessed weapons, and, last but not least, 4d20 damage
for silver damage.

I did that recently; it is quite fun to wipe Orcus out in a single
attack.


